From: =?UTF-8?q?Juan=20Manuel=20L=C3=B3pez=20Carrillo?=
 <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 18:49:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 116/143] pci: sunxi: restore INTx and eDMA interrupt masks on
 resume
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

sunxi_pcie_plat_suspend() tears the controller down through
sunxi_pcie_plat_hw_deinit() (PHY exit, clocks gated, power off), so on
resume the application registers are back at their power-on defaults,
which mask everything (SII_INT_MASK0 default 0x0 per the T527 user
manual, section 8.13.5.32).  The resume path reprogrammed the RC
config space and the MSI target, but never restored:

 - the INTx enable bits in SII_INT_MASK0 that
   sunxi_allocate_intx_domains() writes at probe -- endpoints using
   legacy interrupts lose them silently after a suspend/resume cycle;
 - the eDMA interrupt unmask (PCIE_DMA_WR/RD_INT_MASK = 0) that
   sunxi_pcie_plat_dma_init() writes at probe -- any eDMA transfer
   started after resume would never signal completion.

Mirror both probe-time writes in the RC resume path, after the RC
setup and before the link is re-established.  The vendor BSP 5.15 has
the same gap.

Signed-off-by: Juan Manuel López Carrillo <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: AI Agent
---
 drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-plat.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-plat.c b/drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-plat.c
index 221ef49b2..a9c87429d 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-plat.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-plat.c
@@ -1189,6 +1189,7 @@ static int sunxi_pcie_plat_resume(struct device *dev)
 	struct platform_device *pdev = to_platform_device(dev);
 	struct sunxi_pcie *pci = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 	struct sunxi_pcie_port *pp = &pci->pp;
+	u32 val;
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = sunxi_pcie_plat_hw_init(pci);
@@ -1223,6 +1224,24 @@ static int sunxi_pcie_plat_resume(struct device *dev)
 						    upper_32_bits(msi_target));
 		}
 
+		/*
+		 * Suspend gated the controller clocks (and possibly the
+		 * power domain), so the SII and eDMA interrupt masks are
+		 * back at their power-on default: everything masked.
+		 * Restore what probe programmed, or INTx and eDMA
+		 * completion interrupts stay silently dead after resume:
+		 * - the INTx enables written by
+		 *   sunxi_allocate_intx_domains();
+		 * - the eDMA interrupt unmask written by
+		 *   sunxi_pcie_plat_dma_init().
+		 */
+		val = sunxi_pcie_readl(pci, SII_INT_MASK0);
+		val |= INTX_RX_ASSERT_MASK;
+		sunxi_pcie_writel(val, pci, SII_INT_MASK0);
+
+		sunxi_pcie_writel_dbi(pci, PCIE_DMA_OFFSET + PCIE_DMA_WR_INT_MASK, 0x0);
+		sunxi_pcie_writel_dbi(pci, PCIE_DMA_OFFSET + PCIE_DMA_RD_INT_MASK, 0x0);
+
 		sunxi_pcie_host_establish_link(pci);
 		sunxi_pcie_host_speed_change(pci, pci->link_gen);
 		break;
-- 
